<h2>Problems with Missing Information</h2>
<h3>Warm-up Giant Cantaloupe</h3><p>A normal melon weighs1–5kg. Make three reasoned TOO LOW, ABOUT RIGHT, TOO HIGH estimates for source giant melon. Teacher may reveal actual source winner weight <strong>344kg</strong> AFTER estimates.</p>
<h3>Activity1: Info Gap Pumpkin Weigh-Off</h3><p>Teacher gives each pair two original Problem/Data card sets (1 then2). Source maths involve MULTIPLICATION/DIVISION. Do not expose cards to partner before they ask for needed information, explain why, then both solve. Pause for teacher review, SWAP roles for second set.</p>
<h3>Activity2: Info Gap Pig Weigh-Off</h3><p>Same routine on two new original Pig source sets, now ADDITION/SUBTRACTION of weights. Original numbers are teacher-card data, not in accessible local source text.</p>
<p><strong>Information-gap steps:</strong> privately read assigned card; ask “Can you tell me…?”; reply “Why do you need to know…?”; justify; disclose just relevant fact; repeat until enough data; solve separately; compare; reverse roles.</p>
